on the shoreline at Prestwick beach 14  years ago this month the body of a  Swedish woman was found face down in the  sand the death of 30 year old Annie  Boursin was recorded as suicide her  family on so sure an eight-part  investigation by the sky news podcast  series three cast has looked into the  life and mysterious death of Annie  Boursin the post-mortem conducted in  Scotland recorded the cause of Annie's  death as drowning there were minor  injuries on her body but police were  satisfied they had been caused by coming  into contact with rough objects in the  water it was only when Annie's body was  returned to Sweden that Undertaker's  made a discovery that shocked her family  the Bruce to the head and indicate that  she had been done hardened by someone  investigative journalist marchello mega  is one of few people to have seen  Annie's post-mortem photographs it was a  massive bruise to the temple and which  immediately said to me that she had been  struck very hard probably by a blunt  instrument the sort of blow that would  knock most people unconscious I would  think and there was also significant  bruising to her arms on the day she was  last seen Annie had traveled to preswick  airport from Edinburgh where she lived  she had her passport and entered the  airport terminal building not left  without buying a ticket standing by the  water's edge and looking out to sea  Andrew Montgomery told police at the  time he thought the figure he'd seen on  a distant shore line was a woman 14  years on reflections don't fit the  conclusion it was Annie it's really  unreflecting I think the light was still  Perla I couldn't be absolutely certain  it was a woman  Scotland's grown officer said Annie's  death was thoroughly investigated after  detailed consideration of the facts and  circumstances it says the Procurator  Fiscal concluded there were no  suspicious circumstances and as there  were no systemic defects which  contributed to the death  there was no basis to hold a fatal  accident inquiry Annie's family say it  leaves fundamental questions unanswered  about just what did happen to their  daughter in the moments before her death  here 14 years ago James Matthews Sky  News Prestwick
 

